\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, let us with our Lord arise,
\par Our Lord, who made both earth
\par and skies;
\par Who died to save the world He made,
\par And rose triumphant from the dead;
\par He rose, the Prince of life and peace;
\par And stamped the day for ever His.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. This is the day the Lord hath made,
\par That all may see His love displayed,
\par May feel His resurrection's power,
\par And rise again to fall no more,
\par In perfect righteousness renewed,
\par And filled with all the life of God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Then let us render Him His own,
\par With solemn prayer approach the
\par throne,
\par With meekness hear the gospel word,
\par With thanks His dying love record;
\par Our joyful hearts and voices raise,
\par And fill His courts with songs of 
\par praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Honour and praise to Jesus pay
\par Throughout His consecrated day;
\par Be all in Jesu's praise employed,
\par Nor leave a single moment void;
\par With utmost care the time improve,
\par And only breathe His praise and love.
\par                                   Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

